1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,300
In Brazil, the agency
requires a guarantee.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,550
When tenants don't pay,

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:09,950
agencies cover it or manage the risk.
Other solutions take up to 60 days.

4
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:12,600
MUTAV backs the agency, on Solana.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
19 agencies tested our platform
and signed letters of intent.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,600
Let's register a MUTAV guarantee
for Ana's lease: R$18,000.

7
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:26,500
On-chain, she's just an ID,
no personal data.

8
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:33,700
The reserve holds BRS, a Brazilian
stablecoin from Nora Finance,

9
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:37,000
and anyone can check

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,700
it meets the coverage
the reserve admin sets.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,800
Let's try one more lease.
That needs R$45,000; we have R$44,500.

12
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:48,400
Refused.

13
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,000
We can't promise
what we can't back.

14
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:00,200
Say Ana misses rent.

15
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,600
Our operator files a claim,

16
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,600
the reserve pays, within
the multisig's monthly limit,

17
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:14,700
and the landlord's PIX
is recorded on-chain.

18
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,400
Filed to paid, on-chain:
65 seconds.

19
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,200
Not 60 days.

20
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,900
Today, our operator
signs each step.

21
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:33,000
Next, the agency platform
does it automatically,

22
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,600
inside limits
the program already enforces.

23
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,200
Let's fast-forward: six months
of our pilot plan, simulated locally,

24
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,600
growing the reserve
to R$1 million.

25
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:52,900
Guarantee fees and yield come in.
Small claims go out.

26
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,400
So the reserve can back more leases,

27
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:02,400
and the capital behind it gets back
more than it put in.

28
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:08,200
The reserve that protects agencies
also pays its backers.

29
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:10,200
Check it on Solana.

30
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,600
MUTAV: a reserve you can see,

31
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:16,600
payments that run themselves,
and capital that works.

32
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:18,900
Brazil's on-chain rent guarantee.
